Subject: [PATCH] settings_ui, secret_vault: a Secrets page -- the vault's
 first slice
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The operator's ask (i), 2026-11-22: credentials and secrets in the
settings window. Hub docs/SECRETS-VAULT-PAGE.md, the first slice of
docs/ZEO-NEXT-PROPOSAL.md §6.53's vault; the proxy injection is later.

New crate secret_vault:
- SecretRef: azukari's `service` and `account` attributes. The URI is
  secret://SERVICE/ACCOUNT, split at the first `/`, so an account may hold
  more. A service with `/`, an empty part, surrounding spaces or a control
  character are refused: an attribute with a space is a different item.
- store/list/delete on the Secret Service through oo7 (async-std,
  native_crypto, as gpui_linux's credentials), on the background executor.
  Items carry service, account and zeo-vault=1; the page lists and deletes
  only those. A save replaces an item with the same attributes, so the
  vault never makes the second item azukari would refuse as ambiguous.
- A listing keeps only tail(): the value's last three characters, by
  character. The value itself is never kept.
- Not Linux: list is empty, store and delete say the vault needs the
  Secret Service.

settings_ui, a "Secrets" sub-page after Agent Memory (no settings key:
nothing is written to settings.json):
- the rows show the reference and •••tail ("locked" when the item could not
  be read), with Copy Reference and Delete;
- the service, account and value fields, the page's own editors, and a
  Save button that reads all three when clicked -- a field that confirmed
  on focus-out lost what was typed when the click went straight to the
  next field (seen in the Xvfb proof); the value is cleared at once,
  saved or not, so it is visible only while typed;
- the line to paste into an MCP server entry: `azukari --env NAME --
  <server>`, with NAME set to the reference in the entry's env;
- each outcome as a banner, and one structured log line per store or
  delete, naming the reference, never the value.

Tests: secret_vault_tests (the URI round trip with a `/` in the account;
the references azukari could not resolve the same way are refused; the
attribute set; the tail by character; the azukari command line) and
secrets_page_tests (Save takes the trimmed reference or says why not; a row
shows the reference and only the tail). test.sh gains secret_vault.

Against a real Secret Service: tests/live_keyring.rs (ignored unless
ZEO_VAULT_LIVE=1) stores two secrets, lists them by tail, replaces one --
one item stays -- and deletes both, on a throwaway oo7-daemon over a
private bus (the lab's azukari image), never the operator's keyring.
